  "id": "COMPOUND:24651 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(1R,2S,3R,4S,7R,9S,10S,11R,12R,15R,16S)-2,4,9,11,12,15-hexaacetyloxy-1-hydroxy-10,14,17,17-tetramethyl-6-oxatetracyclo[11.3.1.03,10.04,7]heptadec-13-en-16-yl] benzoate is associated with HepG2 cells through a multi-step pathway. The compound is identified as a target of three different compounds—Oxytroflavoside B, Tubotaiwine, and Cocosamide B—each of which is itself a target of HepG2. This suggests that the compound may act as a potential modulator of HepG2 cell function, possibly through interactions with VMRC-LCP, a protein that is a target of all three compounds. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent relationship between the compound and HepG2, with varying scores reflecting the strength of the association. The mechanism likely involves the compound interacting with VMRC-LCP, which in turn influences HepG2 cells, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The findings support the possibility that the compound could be a candidate for further investigation in the context of HepG2-related therapeutic applications.",
